The chapter in analysed the variation of the synthetic variable defined as the dissemination of responsible management practices and verified its association between:
- location in regions with different levels of development; 
- time of operation in the market; 
- type of ownership capital; 
- size of the company; 
- extent of activity. 
Based on the data collected, the relationships between these variables were verified and their strength estimated using Cramer's V. Responsible management practices are part of the broader area of corporate social responsibility. In the studies carried out, despite the limitations related to their generalisation to the population of all enterprises in Poland, one can note similar to global trends in the dissemination of practices, which represent an ongoing change in the objectives and tasks that stakeholders put before enterprises.
